  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.Conflict">On conflicts</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.KeepBoth">Keep both, rename the local version</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Newer">Take the version changed last</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Older">Take the version changed first</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Local">Always take the local version</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Remote">Always take the remote version</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.ConflictHint">A conflict arises when both sides changed the same file without knowing about the other change. When renaming, both versions stay in the folder: the remote version keeps the name, the local one gets the modification time and the device name appended — photo.sync-conflict-20260901-101656-PC111.jpg. With the other settings, one version stays in the folder; the other is put under .stversions, provided that keeping replaced versions is switched on.</s:String>

  <s:String x:Key="M.PreviewShort">{0} images, {1}</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.KeepVersions">Keep replaced versions</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionsHint">When a file is replaced by the remote version or deleted at its request, the version held here moves to the folder “.stversions” inside the share. That folder takes no part in synchronisation. Placeholders without content are not kept, because there is nothing to save.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionDays">Keep deleted files for … days (0 = delete at once)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionDaysHint">After this time a kept version is removed. Counting starts on the day it was put aside, not from its modification time.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S2.DaysInvalid">The retention time must be 0 or greater.</s:String>
