  <s:String x:Key="M.MarkerRestored">“{0}”: folder marker restored.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="M.FixMarkerTitle">Restore folder marker</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="M.FixMarkerBody">The folder marker is missing in “{0}”.&#10;{1}&#10;&#10;This usually means something is wrong with the folder: a storage medium is not mounted — an external drive, a network share, a memory card — or the folder was renamed or moved.&#10;&#10;Check the folder first. Confirm only once it is certain that this is the right folder and its contents are complete.&#10;&#10;Confirming resumes synchronisation. From then on, files and folders missing here count as deleted, and that deletion is passed on to the other devices.&#10;&#10;Restore the marker now?</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="M.Resyncing">“{0}” is being resynchronised: {1} remote device(s) asked.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S2.ResyncAsk">Discard everything known about this folder from the remote devices and ask again?&#10;&#10;Files are not touched. The index is rebuilt, and until it is complete the folder counts as not synchronised.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.SharedFolders">Shared folders</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.SharedFoldersHint">Ticked is what this device takes part in. The same setting appears in the folder under “Sharing” — per device here, per folder there.</s:String>
